{"name":"Under the Weather","hex":"#aea1aa","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"under the weather","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["ill or gloomy, especially from a cold or flu.","Somewhat intoxicated or suffering from a hangover."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under_the_weather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Under the Weather (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Under the Weather\" is an alternative rock song performed by Scottish singer-songwriter KT Tunstall. The song was written by Tunstall and TommyD and produced by Steve Osborne for Tunstall's debut album Eye to the Telescope (2004). It was released as the album's fourth single on 5 December 2005. The song reached No. 39 on the UK Singles Chart, remaining on the chart for two weeks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/50/Under_the_Weather.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Weather_(song)","wikidata":"Q4004589"},{"title":"Under the Weather (short story)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Under the Weather\" is a short story by Stephen King, originally published in the 2011 paperback edition of Full Dark, No Stars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Weather_(short_story)","wikidata":"Q7883422"},{"title":"Weather","blocks":[{"text":"Weather is the state of the Earth's atmosphere at a specific place and time, typically described in terms of temperature, humidity, cloud cover, and stability. On Earth, most weather phenomena occur in the lowest layer of the planet's atmosphere, the troposphere, just below the stratosphere. Weather refers to day-to-day temperature, precipitation, and other atmospheric conditions, whereas climate is the term for the averaging of atmospheric conditions over longer periods of time. When used without qualification, \"weather\" is generally understood to mean the weather of Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/330px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weather","wikidata":"Q11663"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Under_the_Weather.jpg/250px-Under_the_Weather.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/50/Under_the_Weather.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Under_the_Weather.jpg/250px-Under_the_Weather.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnder_the_Weather.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/500px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/1280px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/500px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thunderstorm near Port-la-Nouvelle, Occitania, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APort_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://th